+@startuml
+title M-LR2 - Artifact ownership, transport and cleanup boundaries
+skinparam componentStyle rectangle
+
+package "CURRENT interactive API - SPEC 0.5.0-draft" {
+  folder "Launcher config - persistent\ncontract owner: curator-run\nfile identity: configuration-directory owner" as config {
+    artifact "defaults.json\nmodel / effort / permissions / host\noperator first unless machine lock" as defaults
+    artifact "ax.json\ntracking switch\nmachine first" as axconfig
+  }
+  folder "Curator-owned persistent context" as context {
+    artifact "Profile / lock / current selection" as profile
+    folder "Managed home\nmarker-recorded prompt / MCP surfaces\nCurator materializes / repairs / garbage collects" as home
+  }
+  folder "curator-run - caller identity\ntransient invocation only" as launcher {
+    artifact "Closed fragment v1 / v2 / v3\nCCJ-1 digest; profile pin\nreserved path_prepend remains non-operative" as fragment
+    artifact "Admitted / composed plan value\nBinary / Argv / Env / Stdin / WorkDir\nno persisted launcher session record" as plan
+    artifact "ax request - generated stdin bytes\nargv suffix, owned literals, lookup names\nencoded stdin, Curator extensions\nNOT full inherited environment" as axpayload
+    artifact "Hosted 1.0.0 payload - private stdin\nfull env / cwd / binary / argv / home\ncontent digest / exec guard / restart / resume metadata\n1 MiB object limit" as hostedpayload
+    artifact "Optional native network snapshot\nprivate read-only evaluated executable\nprocess owner stages and executes same bytes" as snapshot
+  }
+  component "curator env resolve --repair\ncaller-side subprocess" as curator
+  component "Native provider child\ncaller-side identity" as native
+  component "ax start subprocess\ndestination UID unspecified in spec 4.6" as ax
+  database "ax Session Record\nax-owned persistent extensions / session" as record
+  component "task-board receiver subprocess\ndestination UID unspecified in spec 4.9" as receiver
+  artifact "Hosted FD3 = controlling terminal\nHosted FD4 = bounded status pipe\nlauncher copies close-on-exec; receiver ingress clear\nreceiver sets close-on-exec before descendants" as hostfds
+  config --> launcher : validated reads; unsafe / failed read refuses, never absence
+  profile --> curator : resolve selected profile / pin
+  curator --> home : repair ownership; launcher never writes
+  curator --> fragment : closed JSON stdout; foreign stderr preserved
+  fragment --> plan : context channels / owned env / metadata
+  home --> launcher : late Codex layer / prompt read probes only
+  plan --> native : full composed env / cwd / argv / exact stdin
+  plan --> axpayload : literals-only transport
+  axpayload --> ax : stdin is request, not child stdin
+  ax --> record : copied extensions; destination manages session / resume
+  plan --> hostedpayload : same in-hand admitted plan only
+  hostedpayload --> receiver : private stdin
+  hostfds --> receiver : separate terminal / refusal transport
+  snapshot --> native : optional admitted direct network scope
+  note bottom of launcher
+    [[../SPEC.md#47-the-launchers-configuration-file-family SPEC 4.7]] / [[../SPEC.md#41-obtain-the-fragment-context-plane SPEC 4.1]] / [[../SPEC.md#45-compose-the-launch SPEC 4.5]] / [[../SPEC.md#46-hand-off-and-exec SPEC 4.6]] / [[../SPEC.md#49-hosted-payload-and-receiver-handoff SPEC 4.9]].
+    Missing / unreadable Codex layer refuses; retry starts a new Curator repair.
+    Payload / config / channel failure never silently drops metadata or tracking.
+    Invocation buffers / descriptors are not persistent session state.
+    Exact native snapshot removal / hosted durable layout: unspecified in spec 4.4b / 4.9.
+    Tracked destination environment filtering remains open (SPEC 9).
+  end note
+}
+
+package "TARGET one-shot - NOT IMPLEMENTED; dispatcher v0 local headless" {
+  artifact "Caller-owned immutable composed plan\nprofile pin / approved harness identity / effective env / PATH\nprotected tools -> admitted base PATH -> protected dispatcher\nno repository .agents/bin; digest covers resolved PATH" as immutable
+  folder "Dispatcher-owned persistent execution state\nv0 detached supervisor; v1 daemon later" as dispatchstate {
+    artifact "Claims / run and effect IDs\nrequest / agent / execution IDs remain distinct\nper-operation retry reuses its own effect ID" as claims
+    artifact "Outcome / helper termination evidence\nnot inferred from caller / sudo exit" as outcome
+  }
+  folder "Root user-manager / launcher-owned state" as rootstate {
+    artifact "Generation ledger\nroot-owned 0644, root-owned directory\nactive (uid,generation); no secrets" as ledger
+    artifact "Approved executor / active owned home checks" as approved
+    artifact "Atomic start receipt BEFORE UID drop\nexecution_id / epoch / pid / start_time / boot_id / session_id\nattempt identity, not readiness" as startreceipt
+  }
+  component "swarma-user-launcher\nroot process; no-argument sudo entry" as root
+  artifact "Privileged stdin request\n80 KiB / 5 s; base64 plan 64 KiB\nother helper 16 KiB / 5 s\ndispatcher v0 96 KiB / 5 s; v1 frame 128 KiB" as request
+  artifact "Fresh pipe FD3 = decoded plan only\n48 KiB; other FDs >2 closed first\nstandard FDs are caller transport, no plan / secrets\nno broker connection crosses UID drop" as planfd
+  component "curator-run exec adapter\nagent UID worker-<label>\nbounded immutable read / verify" as executor
+  folder "Broker-owned persistent state" as brokerstate {
+    artifact "Protected credential_binding/1\npeer uid / generation, profile, harness, account, channel\nendpoint, harness SHA-256, policy generation\nrandom binding_id and generation never reused" as binding
+    artifact "Credential store\nfiles 0600; owner-only directories 0700\nKeychain / Secret Service later" as store
+  }
+  component "swarma-credential-broker\nservice UID unspecified in spec 10.3\nfresh peer-authenticated connection / 64 KiB frames" as broker
+  artifact "works.relux.curator.credential/1\nrequired-understanding METADATA ONLY\nmode / account / channel; no material" as metadata
+  artifact "Execution-scoped leased material\nqualified channel only\nnever plan / argv / files / logs / receipts" as material
+  component "Admitted harness\nagent-side process\nSlice 0 Claude token env channel" as harness
+  artifact "Consumed-plan / credential evidence\ndigest + qualified executor + policy generation\nno secrets; wire / storage unpublished" as consumed
+  immutable --> request : dispatcher admits smallest applicable bound before provisioning
+  request --> root : closed privileged request on stdin
+  ledger --> root : active generation / ownership checks
+  approved --> root : executor path / digest / home checks
+  root --> startreceipt : atomic write; existing receipt refuses second start
+  root --> planfd : reset env / descriptors; decoded plan pipe
+  planfd --> executor : after clear groups / GID / UID drop; no alternate intake
+  immutable --> metadata : metadata within admitted plan
+  metadata --> executor : no endpoint / executable / material selection by profile bytes
+  ledger --> broker : bind / lease / renew active principal check
+  binding --> executor : destination-local check before lease AND harness execution
+  executor --> broker : selected broker source; digest is launch_id correlation only
+  store --> broker : broker is sole rotating-account refresh owner
+  broker --> material : qualified / authorised execution-scoped lease
+  material --> harness : executor injects only admitted release-qualified channel
+  executor --> harness : verify and execute plan values; no repair / compose / defaults
+  executor --> consumed : required evidence; transport unspecified in spec 10.4
+  consumed --> outcome : dispatcher owns record; not stdout or start receipt substitution
+  note right of broker
+    [[../SPEC.md#103-broker-binding-credential-delivery-and-rollout SPEC 10.3]]:
+    unreadable / missing / retired / ambiguous ledger refuses.
+    revoked caller chain blocks new leases / renewals.
+    source conflict / unqualified injection / binding mismatch refuses;
+    no native login fallback. Harness can read its own token.
+    Native per-home is separate: source-policy v1 absence means per-home;
+    v2 requires explicit source; read failure never means absence.
+    Later Codex: external token to per-session app-server,
+    no launch auth.json / broker-mode codex exec; qualification pending.
+    Muse subscription reserved; API-key lane separate.
+  end note
+  note bottom of dispatchstate
+    [[../SPEC.md#104-signals-stop-receipts-and-cleanup SPEC 10.4]]:
+    owned helper exec.stop verifies receipt identity; TERM then KILL;
+    confirmed descendant absence required before claim release / replacement.
+    Dispatcher unbinds then retires, each effect confirmed separately.
+    Separate one-shot identity revocation only after retirement;
+    standing identity revocation is operator-only.
+    Executor owns neither retirement nor identity revocation.
+  end note
+  note bottom of executor
+    [[../SPEC.md#101-immutable-input-descriptor-transport-and-limits SPEC 10.1]] / [[../SPEC.md#102-caller-dispatcher-privileged-launcher-and-executor SPEC 10.2]] / [[../SPEC.md#105-typed-refusals-exit-status-and-activation-questions SPEC 10.5]].
+    Intake envelope / digest placement / dedicated argv: unspecified in spec 10.1.
+    Post-exec receipt transport and renewal / release ownership: unspecified in spec 10.4.
+    Numeric refusal exits / signal encoding: unspecified in spec 10.5.
+    Unknown process evidence is not success or permission to release capacity.
+    Agent home lifecycle: dispatcher via helper; materialization detail unspecified in spec 10.2.
+    SH2 ticket / helper signature publication and donor B activation remain open.
+    No long-session state / resume / remote capability added by this diagram.
+  end note
+}
+@enduml
